    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d142">

                <pb facs="0262" n="192" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg192"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 341.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-09-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 15, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Just at the moment when the mail is about
                    to close authentic information reaches the government that the insurgent forces
                    which have been approaching and menacing Cincinnati and Louisville have receded,
                    and are retreating in Kentucky. The alarm in that quarter has passed.</p>
                <p>The press has already announced that the insurgent army, which has been
                    threatening Washington, Baltimore, and Pennsylvania, evacuated Frederick on the
                    12th instant. I now give you a despatch which has just been received from Major
                    General McClellan, which shows the position of the two armies at the present
                    moment.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
